  "rulings": [
    {
      "oracle_id": "95c3976c-33f3-490b-bfd3-7f1af2fe0416",
      "published_at": "2020-06-23",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Chromatic Orrery's last ability can have you draw at most five cards. \"Colorless,\" \"artifact,\" and \"gold\" are not colors."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "4f890d42-e4f1-4eed-aa6c-718865de8927",
      "published_at": "2017-04-18",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Vizier of the Menagerie lets you look at the top card of your library whenever you want (with one restriction—see below), even if you don't have priority. This action doesn't use the stack. Knowing what that card is becomes part of the information you have access to, just like you can look at the cards in your hand."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "4f890d42-e4f1-4eed-aa6c-718865de8927",
      "published_at": "2017-04-18",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Normally, Vizier of the Menagerie allows you to cast the top card of your library if it's a creature card, it's your main phase, and the stack is empty. If that creature card has flash, you'll be able to cast it any time you could cast an instant, even on an opponent's turn."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "4f890d42-e4f1-4eed-aa6c-718865de8927",
      "published_at": "2017-04-18",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "The top card of your library isn't in your hand, so you can't cycle it, discard it, or activate any of its activated abilities."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "4f890d42-e4f1-4eed-aa6c-718865de8927",
      "published_at": "2017-04-18",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "You may spend mana as though it were mana of any type to cast any creature spell, not just creature spells that you cast from the top of your library."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "4f890d42-e4f1-4eed-aa6c-718865de8927",
      "published_at": "2017-04-18",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If the top card of your library changes while you're casting a spell, playing a land, or activating an ability, you can't look at the new top card until you finish doing so. This means that if you cast the top card of your library, you can't look at the next one until you're done paying for that spell."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "4f890d42-e4f1-4eed-aa6c-718865de8927",
      "published_at": "2017-04-18",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "You'll still pay all costs for that spell, including additional costs. You may also pay alternative costs such as emerge or that of As Foretold."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "1e94e647-9150-4b22-aa9f-d195f64fb20a",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If an effect allows you to cast a spell without paying its mana cost, you can't choose to cast it and pay unless another rule or effect allows you to cast that spell for a cost. Similarly, you can't waive a cost reduction unless that effect says you may."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "1e94e647-9150-4b22-aa9f-d195f64fb20a",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If an instant or sorcery spell has an adamant ability, you perform the spell's instructions in order. You don't perform the adamant instruction before the spell resolves or before any other effects printed above it."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "1e94e647-9150-4b22-aa9f-d195f64fb20a",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If you copy a spell that has an adamant ability, no mana was spent to cast the copy at all, so that ability won't apply."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "1e94e647-9150-4b22-aa9f-d195f64fb20a",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Adamant effects check what mana was actually spent to cast a spell. If an effect allows you to spend mana “as though it were mana” of any color or type, that allows you to spend mana you couldn't otherwise spend, but it doesn't change what mana you spent to cast the spell."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "cfc8372f-13b6-4628-84c7-066881b287f5",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If a spell with a converge ability is copied, no mana was spent to cast the copy, so the number of colors of mana spent to cast the spell will be zero. The number of colors spent to cast the original spell is not copied."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "cfc8372f-13b6-4628-84c7-066881b287f5",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "The maximum number of colors of mana you can spend to cast a spell is five. Colorless is not a color. Note that the cost of a spell with converge may limit how many colors of mana you can spend."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "cfc8372f-13b6-4628-84c7-066881b287f5",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Unless a spell or ability allows you to, you can't choose to pay more mana for a spell with a converge ability just to spend more colors of mana. Likewise, if a spell or ability reduces the amount of mana it costs you to cast a spell with converge, you can't ignore that cost reduction in order to spend more colors of mana."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "cfc8372f-13b6-4628-84c7-066881b287f5",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If you cast a spell with converge without spending any mana to cast it (perhaps because an effect allowed you to cast it without paying its mana cost), then the number of colors spent to cast it will be zero."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "cfc8372f-13b6-4628-84c7-066881b287f5",
      "published_at": "2015-08-25",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If there are any alternative or additional costs to cast a spell with a converge ability, the mana spent to pay those costs will count. For example, if an effect makes sorcery spells cost {1} more to cast, you could pay {W}{U}{B}{R} to cast Radiant Flames and deal 4 damage to each creature."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "0baabe39-72ae-47bd-a095-cbf7eb8a6361",
      "published_at": "2009-02-01",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Mana produced by Ancient Ziggurat can be spent on any part of a creature spell's total cost. This includes additional costs (such as kicker) and alternative costs (such as evoke or Worldheart Phoenix's alternative cost)."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "0baabe39-72ae-47bd-a095-cbf7eb8a6361",
      "published_at": "2009-02-01",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Mana produced by Ancient Ziggurat can't be spent on activated abilities that put a creature card directly onto the battlefield, such as unearth or ninjutsu."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "ba284fe6-bb29-455c-8321-9714a0cdc05e",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "This mana may be used on additional costs to cast the spell, such as Kicker."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "ba284fe6-bb29-455c-8321-9714a0cdc05e",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "You can spend the mana on costs on the spell's text."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "ba284fe6-bb29-455c-8321-9714a0cdc05e",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "This mana may not be used to pay costs imposed after the spell is initially cast."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "ba284fe6-bb29-455c-8321-9714a0cdc05e",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "The mana can't be used to pay Echo costs."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "d2d41f12-18d8-473b-9308-3f02d7d791f0",
      "published_at": "2016-06-08",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Humble doesn’t counter abilities that have already triggered or been activated. In particular, casting this spell won’t stop a creature’s ability that says “At the beginning of your upkeep,” “When this creature enters the battlefield,” or similar from triggering."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "d2d41f12-18d8-473b-9308-3f02d7d791f0",
      "published_at": "2016-06-08",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Humble overwrites all previous effects that set the creature’s base power and toughness to specific values. Any power- or toughness-setting effects that start to apply after Humble resolves will overwrite this effect."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "d2d41f12-18d8-473b-9308-3f02d7d791f0",
      "published_at": "2016-06-08",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Effects that modify a creature’s power and/or toughness, such as the effect of Seal of Strength, will apply to the creature no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for any counters that change its power and/or toughness and effects that switch its power and toughness."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "d2d41f12-18d8-473b-9308-3f02d7d791f0",
